      "index": "b1J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 82250877,
      "version": 167,
      "versionNonce": 1567360083,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760394861834,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What it represents\nBlog object represents a collection of authored articles on a\nspecific topic. It is the main container and point of identity.\n\nWhy these choices\nThe title and author are essential for identifying the blog. \nThe posts attribute is the core data it manages. \nThe methods represent the absolute minimum functionality:\ncreating content, publishing the blog to make it visible, and\nretrieving the content.",
      "fontSize": 7.272727272727275,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What it represents\nBlog object represents a collection of authored articles on a specific topic. It is the main container and point of identity.\n\nWhy these choices\nThe title and author are essential for identifying the blog. \nThe posts attribute is the core data it manages. \nThe methods represent the absolute minimum functionality: creating content, publishing the blog to make it visible, and retrieving the content.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
